%result
@title
Data Normalization
@paragraph
The different libraries of a single sample were controlled separately and combined for subsequent analysis after meeting the quality control criteria. By visualizing the cell gene profile, UMI profile, the cell activity and gene expression status of each sample can be assessed. Mitochondrial RNA ratio, RNA quantity and expression can reflect cell activity and quality to some extent. In general, the lower the proportion of mitochondrial RNA, the higher the number of RNA, and the higher the expression of RNA, the better the activity and quality of cells.
@figure
number = 2
title = "Scatter plot of mRNA and mitochondrial RNA correlation"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/02.Normalize/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_fig1_scatterplot.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 768>
desc="Each dot represents a cell. Left: X axis represents mRNA expression, Y axis represents the proportion of mitochondrial RNA; Right: mRNA expression on the X-axis and mRNA number on the Y-axis. The numbers in the figure represent the correlation system."

@figure
number = 3
title = "QC violin diagram"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/02.Normalize/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_fig1_vlnplot.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 768>
desc="Left: mRNA number; Middle figure: mRNA expression; Right: Mitochondrial RNA ratio."


@paragraph
According to the quantitative results, the data was filtered out, and the cells with too low or too high mRNA expression and too high proportion of mitochondrial RNA were filtered out. For details, see the information analysis flow - Data Quality Control and Filtering. After filtering, the expression levels of all genes in the cells were homogenized for subsequent analysis.
%result
@title
High variable gene selection and PCA dimensionality reduction
@paragraph

@subtitle
number = 1
 Highly variable feature screening 
@paragraph
 Based on the mean and dispersion (mean and variance) of all genes in each sample, R-package -Seurat\reference{4} was used to screen out genes with high variability in each sample for downstream PCA analysis. The 2,000 genes with the highest degree of variation are selected by default. See Information Analysis Flow - High Variable Feature Screening for details.
@figure
number = 4
title = "High variant gene screening plot"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/03.HvgPCA/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_fig3_var.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 860>
desc="The X-axis represents the average expression level, and the Y-axis represents the standardized variance. On the basis of the left figure, marker genes with the top 10 expression level variation were marked in the right figure."


@subtitle
number = 2
 Principl component analysis 
@paragraph
 Dimensional heat maps show the heterogeneity of principal component (PC) genes with the greatest variation and their expression levels in cell data, helping to select appropriate dimensions for downstream analysis. You can also use the elbow plot to determine how many PCS are used to cluster in order to capture most of the changes in the data. Figure 5 and Figure 6 are used to show the dimension reduction results of top15PC. It can be seen that with the increase of PC components, features become less and less obvious, which is helpful for downstream selection of appropriate dimensions.
@figure
number = 5
title = "Dimension reduction heatmap for Top15 PCS"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/03.HvgPCA/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_fig3_pca.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 1200>
desc="Each column represents a cell and each row represents a gene; Yellow indicates high expression and purple indicates low expression."

@figure
number = 6
title = "Elbow plot for Top15 PCS"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/03.HvgPCA/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_fig3_elbowplot.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 768>
desc="The X-axis is the PC serial number and the Y-axis is the standard deviation."

%result
@title
Data Clean
@paragraph
Different libraries of a single sample were cleaned and filtered separately, and then combined for subsequent analysis after meeting the quality control standards. By calculating the possible proportion of double cells (nuclear) in the droplet and the possible foreign RNA contamination, the cells most likely to be contaminated or double cells (nuclear) were inferred by hypothesis testing under a certain probability. The results of the calculation are presented by the dimensionality reduction cluster plot of the data, and the cells eliminated by both filtering methods are eliminated and not included in the subsequent analysis.
@figure
number = 7
title = "Doublets (nuclear) and Singlets cells identified by DoubletFinder."
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/04.Decontamination/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_doublets_dimplot.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 768>
desc="Each dot represents a cell. Different colors indicate cell types; red indicates that the cell is Doublets (nuclear) and cyan indicates that the cell is Singlets. "

@figure
number = 8
title = "DecontX identifies contaminated cells."
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/04.Decontamination/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_decontx_class.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 768>
desc="Each dot represents a cell. Different colors indicate cell types, with red indicating a higher probability of cell contamination and cyan indicating a lower probability of cell contamination."


@paragraph
According to the quantitative results, the data were filtered out, and the cells that might be double (nuclear) or with contamination were filtered out. The filtered data set was used to homogenize the expression levels of all genes in the cells for subsequent analysis.
%result
@title
Single sample analysis
@paragraph
@subtitle
number = 1
 Cell Clustering 
@paragraph
 Firstly, PCA was used for dimensionality reduction of gene expression matrix, and then UMAP was used for cell clustering. The cell clustering results were shown in Figure 6. In this figure, each point represents a cell, and the closest points in space indicate that the gene expression patterns of these cells are more similar. The colors are determined by a graph-based clustering algorithm that identifies cells within a cluster as having the most similar gene expression patterns.
@figure
number = 9
title = " Cell clustering result"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/04.sSample/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_fig4_cluster.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 768>
desc="The X-axis represents the first component of UMAP, and the Y-axis represents the second component of UMAP. The number and color represent the cluster number."


@subtitle
number = 2
 Marker gene identification 
@paragraph
 Seurat was used to calculate the differentially expressed genes (marker genes) between each type of cell and other groups. After screening and correction, top10 marker genes with p-value<0.05 and log2FC(log2 fold change: used to evaluate the average expression difference multiple) were used for visualization of subsequent results. Table 4 shows the first five rows of results. The complete table is in the delivery directory IDBiotech_result/ 4.SINGLE_SAMPLE /*/2.marker_find/*top10_GeneDiffExp.xls.
@table
number = 5
title = "run_count_1kpbmcsMarker genes of cell clustering(Top3)"
file = <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/04.sSample/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_top3_Markers.xls>
format = <field = 1; type = string; align =centre; align =centre; desc = "P-value">
format = <field = 2; type = string; align =centre; desc = "Average log2FC">
format = <field = 3; type = string; align =centre; desc = "pct.1">
format = <field = 4; type = string; align =centre; desc = "pct.2">
format = <field = 5; type = string; align =centre; desc = "Adjusted P-value">
format = <field = 6; type = string; align =centre; desc = "Cluster">
format = <field = 7; type = string; align =centre; desc = "Gene">
footnote = "pct.1: Percentage of Marker cells in the current cell cluster;"
footnote = "pct.2: Percentage of Marker cells in other remaining cell clusters."
footnote = "avg_logFC: A multiple of the difference in the average expression between the two groups is recorded, with a positive value indicating that the feature is expressed more highly in the current cluster."
footnote = "p_val_adj: The adjusted P-value, the smaller of adjusted Pvalue, the more significant it is."
footnote = "cluster: cell clusters."
view = -1


@subtitle
number = 3
 Marker gene identification 
@paragraph
 The obtained Marker genes were statistically expressed in different cell groups, and visualized by means of clustering heat map, bubble map and violin map. The results of Top3 genes in each cell group were shown in figure10, figure11 and figure12, respectively.
