%result
@title
Annotation of Cell Clusters
@paragraph
After dividing cells into different groups through cluster analysis, cell types are further identified by using marker gene information in public databases.
SingleR Cell Annotation
SingleR\reference{4}can recognize the existing cell clustering results based on Seurat, compare each cluster with a reference data set, and score the cluster according to the similarity of gene expression between cluster and known cell groups in the reference data set to obtain a scoring matrix. Cells/Bins can be annotated into different groups by scoring matrix results. The visualization results of the scoring matrix of cell clustering results are shown in Figure 15, and the annotation results of cell groups are shown in Figure 16.
@figure
number = 15
title = "Scoring heatmap of cell cluster annotation by SingleR"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/06.SingleR/run_count_1kpbmcs_Heatmap_singleR.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 768>
desc="x-axis, the cell clusters; y-axis, cell types contained in the reference dataset; the color ranges from blue to yellow, and the more closer to yellow, the higher scores; top lables represent the annotation result by SingleR."
@figure
number = 16
title = "Annotation results of cell clusters by SingleR"
file = <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/06.SingleR/run_count_1kpbmcs_DimPlot_singleR.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 900; height = 350>
desc="Cluster results of UMAP. Each color represents a cell cluster annotaed by SingleR."
%result
@title
Pseudotime Analysis
@paragraph
Pseudotime analysis, also known as trajectory inference, refers to obtaining cell lineage information according to the differentially expressed genes among different cell groups and constructing a change trajectory of cells in a virtual timeline. Based on these results, a cell change timeline can be recreated.
        Monocle3\reference{5} was used for Pseudo-time analysis. Based on the result of dimensionality reduction and clustering, we further estimated whether the clustering results belonged to the same developmental trajectory. The cell groups were visualized according to the developmental trajectories predicted by the software, and the results are shown in Figure 17.
@figure
number = 17
title = "Cell development trajectory diagram"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/07.Monocle/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_track.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 768>
desc="The black lines in the figure show the presumed trajectory of cell development."
@paragraph
According to the results of cell development trajectory, combined with the changes of gene expression levels in different cell groups, Monocle3 could identify the cells at the earliest developmental stage using a machine learning algorithm and create a pseudo-time analysis, as shown in Figure 18.
@figure
number = 18
title = "Diagram of pseudo time series analysis results"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/07.Monocle/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_pseudotime.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 768>
desc="The black lines represent the presumed developmental trajectory of the cells, ranging in color from purple to yellow, and the color closer to yellow, the cells develop the later."
@paragraph
In the clustering results of different cell classes, the top 5 marker genes calculated by Monocle3 were selected, and the gene expression levels were visualized according to the obtained pseudo-time results, as shown in Figure 19.
@figure
number = 19
title = "Pseudo expression result of Marker gene"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/07.Monocle/run_count_1kpbmcs_Cluster_1_monocle.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 768>
desc="x-axis, the result of Pseudotime; y-axis, gene expression, and the color ranges from purple to yellow. the color closer to yellow, the cell development time is the later. The black line shows trends in gene expression."
%result
@title
Interaction of Cell Clusters
@paragraph
CellChat\reference{6} is a tool capable of quantitatively inferring and analyzing cell-to-cell communication networks from single-cell data, using network analysis and pattern recognition methods to predict the main signal inputs and outputs of cells and how these cells and signals coordinate their functions. The CellChatDB database incorporates signal analysis information from KEGG and recent studies. The database includes known ligand-receptor complex compositions, including ligand-receptor polymeric complexes and several coenzyme factors. In this project, CellChat was used to identify ligand/receptor relationships and intercellular communication molecules in spatio-temporal data, and to study the interaction and communication networks between different cell types.The communication network among all cell clusters is shown in Fig20, and the communication network between each cluster and other clusters is shown in Fig21.
@figure
number = 20
title = "Communication network diagram between all cell clusters"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/08.CellChat/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_netall.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 800>
desc="The thicker the connection line, the stronger the interaction between two clusters"
@figure
number = 21
title = "Communication network diagram between each cell cluster and others"
file =  <url = IDBiotech_result/run_count_1kpbmcs/08.CellChat/sample_run_count_1kpbmcs_neteach.png; label = "run_count_1kpbmcs">
size = <width = 800>
desc="The thicker the connection line, the stronger the interaction between two clusters"

